description: Frontend TypeScript conventions
globs: src/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Frontend conventions

- `strict` + `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` are on; no `any`, no non-null `!` on DOM lookups
  (use the `$()` helper which throws on missing elements).
- Only `src/api.ts` imports `@tauri-apps/api`; components call its typed wrappers.
- Render untrusted data (process names, users) with `textContent`, never `innerHTML`.
- Surface every rejected `invoke` in `state.error` via `describeError()`;
  never swallow errors silently.
- Destructive actions need confirmation. Use the inline two-click pattern —
  `window.confirm` is unreliable in Tauri webviews.
- Floating promises are explicit: `void refresh()`.

# i18n (zh / en, follows system language)

- No user-visible literals in TS or HTML. Add the key to `zh` in `src/i18n.ts`;
  `en` is typed as `Messages`, so a missing translation fails `tsc`.
- Static markup uses `data-i18n`, `data-i18n-placeholder`, `data-i18n-title`.
- Dynamic text calls `t().key` at render time (never cache the string).
- Backend errors arrive as `{ code, pid?, detail? }`; add new codes to
  `AppErrorCode` and both `errors` tables.

```ts
// ❌
li.innerHTML = `<b>${entry.processName}</b>`;
button.textContent = "结束";

// ✅
name.textContent = entry.processName;
button.textContent = t().kill;
await killProcess(pid).catch((e) => (state.error = describeError(e)));
```
